{#
/**
 * @file
 * Theme implementation for a Slate form embed.
 *
 * Renders an empty div for Slate's script to write the form into, with a
 * fallback link and a status message beside it.
 *
 * Keep the link and the status message outside the div. Rationale: Slate
 * replaces everything inside that div. For example, if Slate can't fetch the
 * form, it overwrites the div with its own "To complete this form, click
 * here." message, so a link inside would vanish right when someone needs it.
 * The loading spinner goes inside the div for the same reason: the form
 * replaces it.
 *
 * The link goes to the form's plain URL, not the embed URL. Slate answers the
 * embed URL with JavaScript, so a link to it would show a script instead of
 * the form.
 *
 * The link is visible in the markup. The loader hides it once it takes over
 * and shows it again if the form fails, so a browser with no JavaScript,
 * where the embed can't load anyway, still gets it.
 *
 * Available variables:
 * - attributes: (Attribute) Attributes for the div Slate writes into,
 *   including the id we pass to Slate as the embed's "div" parameter.
 * - canonical_url: (string) The form's plain URL, safe to link to.
 */
#}
<div class="az-media-slate">
  <div{{ attributes }}></div>
  <a href="{{ canonical_url }}" class="az-media-slate__fallback" rel="noopener">
    {{ 'Open this form'|t }}
  </a>
  <p class="az-media-slate__status" aria-live="polite"></p>
</div>
